James sought a creative story for his 5-year-old son, who enjoys scary themes like vampires and monsters. Frustrated by overly sappy early reader books, he requested a short, engaging story that includes a bad guy protagonist and trickery, with a structure suitable for a 4-page format. The story was to feature four lines for James to read, written well, and four lines for his son to read, using short words and repetition. The goal was for the entire narrative to fit within these four pages, appealing to his son's interests and reading level.
